/// Registration of custom data component types, and access to their values on item stacks.
///
/// Clients that carry a mod can synchronise registries, among them `minecraft:data_component_type`,
/// and then expect the data components of the mod on every item stack the server sends. Vanilla
/// components are the `data-component` enum, a plugin registers more here. The type registered as
/// the n-th gets the id `get-vanilla-data-component-type-count() + n` (0 for the first type
/// registered by any plugin), and the server never reuses or changes an id while it runs. Plugins
/// that register types must load in a stable order if clients depend on the ids. At most 64 types
/// can be registered.
///
/// # Values
///
/// The value of a custom component is a byte list: its network encoding, exactly the bytes a client
/// reads or writes after the component id in an item stack. The server keeps the bytes and writes
/// them back unchanged, so stacks keep their custom components when they move through inventories,
/// the creative inventory and container packets.
///
/// # Codecs
///
/// Most places in the protocol do not say how long a component value is, so the server has to know
/// the shape of the encoding to find where one ends. Every type is registered with a `codec`, a
/// description of that shape in prefix notation (a list of `codec-op`, one root node that is a
/// primitive, or `optional` / `repeated` / `sequence` followed by the nodes they apply to).
///
/// * A vanilla `VarInt` component is `[var-int]`.
/// * `terminal_size` (two `VarInt`) is `[sequence(2), var-int, var-int]`.
/// * `treasure_disk` (two strings) is `[sequence(2), text, text]`.
/// * `printout` (a string, then a count and that many pairs of strings) is
///   `[sequence(2), text, repeated, sequence(2), text, text]`.
/// * `UpgradeData` (a `VarInt` and a data component patch) is `[sequence(2), var-int,
///   component-patch]`.
///
/// Where a stack is length prefixed on the wire (the stacks clients send) the server does not need
/// the codec to find the end, but it still checks that the bytes are exactly one value of it.
///
/// # Persistence
///
/// A `persistent` type is saved with the stack (in the inventory, a container, an item entity) under
/// its full key as an NBT byte array of the network bytes, and loaded back as long as the type is
/// registered. A type that is not persistent only lives in memory and on the wire.
///
/// # Limits
///
/// The server cannot compute the hash a client sends for a stack in a container click when the stack
/// has custom components, so it counts such a stack as changed and resends the slot. Custom
/// components are invisible to the vanilla data component functions of `item-stack`
/// (`get-components`, `set-component`), use the functions here.
///
/// Registration is only possible until the server starts accepting connections (plugin load and
/// `server-load-event`), and needs the `registry.components` permission.
interface custom-components {
    use item-stack.{item-stack};

    /// One node of the description of a value's network encoding, in prefix notation.
    variant codec-op {
        /// A `VarInt`.
        var-int,
        /// A `VarLong`.
        var-long,
        /// One byte that is `0` or `1`.
        flag,
        /// One byte.
        byte,
        /// Two bytes, big endian.
        short,
        /// Four bytes, big endian.
        int,
        /// Eight bytes, big endian.
        long,
        /// Four bytes, big endian IEEE 754.
        float32,
        /// Eight bytes, big endian IEEE 754.
        float64,
        /// A `VarInt` length and that many bytes of UTF-8. Identifiers are strings too.
        text,
        /// A `VarInt` length and that many bytes.
        byte-array,
        /// 16 bytes.
        uuid,
        /// A fixed number of bytes.
        fixed-bytes(u32),
        /// A network NBT tag (an unnamed root).
        nbt,
        /// An item stack in the play encoding.
        stack,
        /// A data component patch: `VarInt` added, `VarInt` removed, the added `(VarInt id, value)`
        /// pairs, the removed `VarInt` ids. Values of custom components inside it are read with
        /// their own codec.
        component-patch,
        /// A `flag` and, if it is true, the node that follows.
        optional,
        /// A `VarInt` count and that many of the node that follows.
        repeated,
        /// The next `n` nodes in order.
        sequence(u32),
    }

    /// A component type and its network id.
    record component-type-entry {
        /// The full resource location, `namespace:path`.
        key: string,
        id: u32,
        persistent: bool,
    }

    /// Registers a component type and returns its id. `key` is a full resource location,
    /// `namespace:path`, lowercase, `a-z 0-9 _ - .` (and `/` in the path); the `minecraft`
    /// namespace is reserved. Registering the same definition again returns the same id (a reloaded
    /// plugin), a different definition for a known key fails. Fails for an invalid key or codec,
    /// when 64 types are registered, or when registration is closed.
    register-data-component-type: func(key: string, persistent: bool, codec: list<codec-op>) -> result<u32, string>;

    /// Returns the id of a custom component type by key.
    get-data-component-type-id: func(key: string) -> option<u32>;

    /// Returns the number of vanilla data component types. This is also the id of the first custom
    /// type.
    get-vanilla-data-component-type-count: func() -> u32;

    /// Returns all custom component types in id order.
    get-registered-data-component-types: func() -> list<component-type-entry>;

    /// Sets a custom component on an item stack, replacing the one it has. The value has to be
    /// exactly one value of the codec of the type, otherwise this fails and nothing changes.
    set-custom-component: func(stack: borrow<item-stack>, key: string, value: list<u8>) -> result<_, string>;

    /// Returns the value of a custom component of an item stack, none if it has none.
    get-custom-component: func(stack: borrow<item-stack>, key: string) -> option<list<u8>>;

    /// Removes a custom component from an item stack. Fails if the type is not registered.
    remove-custom-component: func(stack: borrow<item-stack>, key: string) -> result<_, string>;
}
